{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.5,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["D1", "D3", "D42", "R78", "R56", "R77"],
      "pins": ["D1.2", "D3.2", "D42.2", "D1.1", "D3.1", "D42.1"],
      "nets": ["/NET0129", "NET0174", "NET0182", "NET0148"],
      "observed": "The anodes of D1, D3 and D42 all sit on /NET0129 and nothing else. That net has no supply connection, so the three status LEDs have no path to +3V3. Their cathodes are driven through R78, R56 and R77 from the CM4 Ethernet and activity LED nets.",
      "expected": "Status LED anodes should be tied to a supply rail, as with the other indicator LEDs in the design (e.g. D24 anode on +3V3, D36 anode via R32 to +3V3), so the LEDs can be driven active-low from the CM4 pins.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"35\") (name \"/NET0129\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"D1\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D3\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D42\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+3V3\")"}
      ],
      "impact": "The Ethernet and activity indicator LEDs D1, D3 and D42 cannot conduct, so these status indications never light.",
      "confidence": 0.4
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["D20", "R76", "U8"],
      "pins": ["D20.4", "D20.2", "R76.1", "R76.2", "U8.4"],
      "nets": ["NET0036", "Net-(D20-K2)"],
      "observed": "D20 pin 4 (A2 anode) and R76 pin 2 both sit on NET0036, which is also driven by U8 pin 4 (Y). R76 runs from the K2 cathode (Net-(D20-K2)) back to that same node. The second LED channel is therefore in a loop with its own driver output and cannot be driven.",
      "expected": "Following the pattern of the other indicator LEDs (anode on a driver node such as NET0086, cathode through a series resistor to the opposite driver or GND), the K2 resistor should return to a different node from the anode drive.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"73\") (name \"NET0036\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"D20\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"A2\") (pintype \"input\")) (node (ref \"J11\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"Pin_6\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"J33\") (pin \"6\") (pinfunction \"Pin_6\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"R76\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"U8\") (pin \"4\") (pinfunction \"Y\") (pintype \"output\")))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"166\") (name \"Net-(D20-K2)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"D20\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"K2\") (pintype \"input\")) (node (ref \"R76\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")))"}
      ],
      "impact": "The K2 channel of the dual LED D20 cannot be lit, and the CAN-connector pin 6 (J11/J33) is also tied to this LED drive node.",
      "confidence": 0.3
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows status LEDs with anodes on an isolated, unpowered net (D1, D3, D42) and a dual-LED channel that loops back onto its own driver node (D20 channel 2). Both look like wiring errors, though the spec does not cover LED wiring, so confidence is moderate."
}

